Type: Package
Package: LLMRpanel
Title: Calibrated Silicon Samples for Survey and Experiment Design
Version: 0.5.0
Authors@R:
    person("Ali", "Sanaei", , "sanaei@uchicago.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Quantitative silicon sampling with calibration as a mandatory
  artifact, built on 'LLMR'. Persona panels are drawn from user-supplied
  population margins; instruments (Likert batteries, forced choices, open
  items, factorial vignettes, conjoint tasks) are administered with item-
  and option-order randomization; every result object carries a calibration
  slot and prints an UNCALIBRATED banner until benchmark comparison fills
  it. The package's stance is printed into its objects: silicon panels are
  design-stage instruments -- for pretesting, piloting, and power analysis --
  and instruments for measuring model behavior; they do not estimate human
  population quantities unless calibration earns that reading.
